: https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1940-08-13/pdf/FR-1940-08-13.pdf\nSHA-256 of the downloaded file: fc4597c24e5adc331baffe286562509cc9ca5b2fde782fba5114b0faf0e4b1df\nLocation: 5 FR 2818, PDF pages 6-6 (confidence low)\nMachine-extracted text layer of the official PDF (OCR for 1936-1994 scans). May contain recognition errors and parts of neighbouring documents on the same pages. Not an authenticated transcription: check the PDF pages.\n\n=== PDF page 6 of 16 ===\n2818 FEDERAL REGISTER, Tuesday , August 13, 1940\n40 Stat. 845, 848 (U.S.C., title 10, sec.  \n1341), it is ordered that, subject to valid  \nexisting rights, all the following-described  \npublic lands be, and they are hereby,  \nwithdrawn from all forms of appropria­\ntion under the public-land laws, including  \nthe mining and leasing laws, for the use  \nof the War Department as an anti­\naircraft firing range:\nTallahassee Meridian\nT. 3 S., R. 31 W.,  \nsec. 24, lot 3;  \nsec. 25, lot 2;  \nsec. 28, lots 1  and 2;  \nsec. 30, lot 2;\n195.26 acres.\nThis order supersedes the withdrawal  \nmade by Executive Order No. 6964 of  \nFebruary 5, 1935, as amended, and Ex­\necutive Order No. 4109 of December 8,  \n1924, as to any of the above-described  \nlands.\nF ranklin  D R oosevelt\nT he W hite  H ouse ,\nAugust 8, 1940.\n[No. 85081\n[F. R. Doc. 40-3329; Filed, August 9, 1940;  \n12:47 p. m.]\nmore or less, in Boone County, Missouri,  \nbe, and it is hereby, transferred to the  \nDepartment of the Interior, and the area ","path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/texts/EO_8509.txt","sha256":"d5762cd5a6f2bde22e9e8ec25d7062e79c26e15a721a03e054ac3680ef50dca4","source":{"line":112,"path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"bd1d5b7faa3518642567f70c6aff8d7b6da65256e204baec27a1b27c6b9d98f1"}}]}
